 ocuses on California native plants that support local wildlife and pollina
 tors—especially butterflies and moths. Whether you’re adding a few nat
 ives to your garden\, creating a backyard wildlife habitat\, or looking fo
 r host and nectar plants\, we’ll have a wide variety to choose from. Fal
 l is an excellent time to plant California native plants. This year’s sa
 le will include red-flowering currant\, seaside daisy\, Douglas iris\, Dut
 chman’s pipevine\, western azalea\, blue elderberry\, tiger lily\, hedge
 row plants\, and much more. Plant lists organized by bloom time and butter
 fly and moth host plants will be available at the sale\, and our knowledge
 able staff will be on hand to help answer questions and help you choose pl
 ants for your garden. Because parking at Hallberg Butterfly Gardens is lim
 ited\, the plant sale is by appointment. Reserve a time and view the compl
 ete 
