BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cajugband.org/festival/", "Press Democrat": "https://cajugband.org/festival/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cajugband.org/festival/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:24th Annual California Jug Band Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
UID:261001yxp4uqc2OEeIUO9h1kwqzQ
DESCRIPTION:The 24th Annual California Jug Band Festival Brings a Century-
 Old American Musical Tradition to Petaluma\n\nFree all-ages music festival
  at Lagunitas Brewing Company features five California jug bands and an op
 en community jam.\n\nPETALUMA\, CA — The California Jug Band Association
  is bringing  the 24th Annual California Jug Band Festival to Petaluma fo
 r the first time on Saturday\, October 3\, with a full day of free music c
 elebrating one of America’s most distinctive and often-overlooked musica
 l traditions.\n\nThe 2026 lineup brings together jug band musicians from t
 hroughout California\, including groups from the North Bay\, East Bay\, an
 d Santa Cruz area. While the participating bands perform in a variety of m
 usical styles throughout the year\, each will be leaning into its jug band
  repertoire for the festival.\n\n12:00–1:10 PM — The Trolley Drops\, S
 anta Cruz\, CA\n\n1:30–2:40 PM — Paradise Park Jug Band\, Santa Cruz\,
  CA\n\n3:00–4:10 PM — Rivertown Skifflers\, Petaluma\, CA\n\n4:30–5:
 40 PM — Washboard Rhythm Co.\, Berkeley\, CA\n\n6:00–7:10 PM — Five 
 Cent Coffee\, Oakland\, CA\n\n7:15–8:00 PM — Open Public Jug Band Jam\
 n\nEVENT INFORMATION\n\n24th Annual California Jug Band Festival\n\nSaturd
 ay\, October 3\, 2026\n\n12:00–8:00 PM\n\nLagunitas Brewing Company\n\n1
 280 N. McDowell Blvd.\n\nPetaluma\, CA\n\nFree admission\; donations welco
 me\n\nAll ages\n\nNo registration required for attendance\n\nFrom noon to 
 8 p.m.\, five California jug bands will perfoarm at Lagunitas Brewing Comp
 any\, 1280 N. McDowell Blvd.\, Petaluma. The festival will feature The Tro
 lley Drops\, Rivertown Skifflers\, Paradise Park Jug Band\, Washboard Rhyt
 hm Co.\, and Five Cent Coffee. Admission is free\, with donations to the C
 alifornia Jug Band Association’s general fund welcomed throughout the da
 y.\n\nThe festival is an all-ages celebration of jug band music—a musica
 l tradition built around community\, improvisation\, and making music with
  whatever is at hand. Washboards\, washtub basses\, kazoos\, harmonicas\, 
 jugs\, and other improvised instruments are as fundamental to the sound as
  more conventional instruments.\n\n“Jug band music is about as unpretent
 ious as music gets\,” said Jared Emerson-Johnson\, President of the Cali
 fornia Jug Band Association’s board of directors. “It grew out of comm
 unities where people made music with what they had\, and it became this in
 credibly creative and joyful tradition. There’s something wonderful abou
 t bringing that spirit into an art loving place like Petaluma\, where the 
 whole community can come together\, listen\, dance\, have a beer\, and may
 be even pick up an instrument and join the jam.”\n\n“We love that this
  festival gives us a chance to see each other and reconnect with the large
 r jug band community in California\,” said Mary McGown\, secretary of th
 e California Jug Band Association. “It’s a pretty unusual thing to hav
 e this much jug band music in one place\, played by so many of the musicia
 ns who love this tradition. And then at the end of the day\, everybody get
 s to play together.”\n\nThe festival will conclude with an open Jug Band
  Jam from 7:15 to 8 p.m.\, inviting musicians and members of the public to
  join in. Dancers and listeners are welcome throughout the day\, and infor
 mational stations will offer attendees an opportunity to learn more about 
 the history of the musical tradition.\n\nThe full Lagunitas Brewing Compan
 y kitchen and taproom will be open during the festival\, and on-site parki
 ng will be available in the brewery’s regular parking area. Covered spac
 e will be available in the event of rain.\n\nAll proceeds raised through f
 estival donations will support the California Jug Band Association’s ong
 oing work to promote and preserve jug band music\, fund future festivals\,
  and support additional community music events. The organization hopes eve
 ntually to expand its activities to include satellite jug band festivals a
 nd gatherings throughout California.
LOCATION:Lagunitas Brewing Company
URL:https://cajugband.org/festival/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
