BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108769759?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Lou Hazel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
UID:260910jHE4BVf1I0m44p7c9BUCzg
DESCRIPTION:Lou Hazel was born in the town of Olean\, New York to a family
  of northeastern wiseacres.\n\nNot one to commit\, he skirted the compulsi
 ve hunting and fishing tradition held close to his father’s heart - inst
 ead cultivating a sensitivity more suited to artists and vagabonds. As a r
 esult\, his travels brought him across the country and eventually through 
 debilitating depression before coming to rest with a sense of personal pea
 ce and positivity in Durham\, NC.\n\nYet\, Lou’s brain is still a bat ca
 ve. Mostly\, he wakes up with no idea what he’s going to do next\, then 
 finds himself there. In songwriting\, he pulls from this cave rambling\, h
 eartfelt tales flowing through unselfconscious truth. In illustrations\, h
 e swirls and meanders towards an eventual finish only understood upon comp
 letion – as in his music. And in his photography and design work\, he re
 nders the essence of fellow musicians into expressive\, personalized works
  of art.\n\nToday\, Louie continues crafting genuine folk tales of honest 
 longing\, disquieting loss\, and nostalgia through a brilliant sheen of fr
 esh insight with humble humor. Grabbing us by the ears in a new-age\, Prin
 e-like grip. Transforming the minutiae of everyday life into ever more evo
 cative music. And surprising us all\, including himself\, with where we em
 erge.\n\nIn other words\, Lou Hazel is coming out of this unbearable\, unb
 elievably tragic\, disconcerting year like a damn newborn moth with jet en
 gine wings aimed toward a totally full super-moon. And it is good.
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108769759?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/illeagles-103-p248.aspx", "Press Democrat": "https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/illeagles-103-p248.aspx"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/illeagles-103-p248.aspx"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:ILLEAGLES - The Premier Tribute to the Music of the Eagles
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T200000
UID:260822JbYaY8Mxk0qUa7MdXdTFjQ
DESCRIPTION:**Date:** Saturday\, October 3\, 2026\n\n**Time:** Doors 6 P
 M | Show 8 PM\n\n**Tickets:** $35\n\n**Food Vendor:** TBA\n\nWhat do peop
 le want when they go see a live band? The members of SF Bay Area based tri
 bute band ILLEAGLES believe that everyone in the crowd wants to be engaged
  and captivated from the first note until the show is done. Over the past 
 year and a half of sold out performances\, that is exactly what every crow
 d has gotten.\n\nILLEAGLES was founded in late 2016 when 6 friends came to
 gether who all had 2 things in common: 1) they loved the music of the Eagl
 es\, and 2) each member was an amazing musician in their own right. This c
 ommon vision led to hours and hours of studying\, rehearsing\, and masteri
 ng each of the Eagles classic hits.\n\nFrom rockers Life in the Fast Lane 
 and Heartache Tonight\, to swooning ballads Desperado and Best of My Love\
 , ILLEAGLES not only reproduce the soaring guitars\, multi-part harmonies 
 and tightness of the original band\, but also add their own brand of swagg
 er and energy that keeps fans coming back over and over. It's commonplace 
 for a majority of the audience to start singing along on the first song\, 
 and continuing to sing until the show is over (or they lose their voices).
 \n\nILLEAGLES- A high energy\, unforgettable party that leaves fans wantin
 g more...
LOCATION:Coyote Sonoma
URL:https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/illeagles-103-p248.aspx
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
