X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Napa Valley Museum Yountville FREE Oct 3-4 Bank of America Museums
  on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T160000
UID:260928estgi7Eti0OH7HSFmDxldQ
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is October 3-4. \n\nAs a chill settles in the air\, Halloween
  costumes are planned\, and leaves crunch on the ground\, take a moment th
 is busy fall season to enjoy a very special exhibit in your own backyard! 
 The Napa Valley Museum Yountville has exciting exhibits including Mary Bla
 ir: Mid-Century Magic\, a special exhibition by the Walt Disney Family Mus
 eum exploring the creative vision and achievements of one of Walt Disney
 ’s most imaginative and renowned designers and art directors. Mary’s w
 ork appeared in classic Disney animated films like Cinderella \\(1950\\)\,
  Alice in Wonderland \\(1951\\)\, and Peter Pan \\(1953\\). The exhibit cl
 oses October 25\, 2026\, so it might be your last chance to make it before
  it’s gone!\n\nBank of America Museums on Us program offers FREE weekend
  general admission on the first full weekend of every month to Bank of Ame
 rica\, Merrill and Bank of America Private Bank credit and debit cardholde
 rs. All you need is your Bank of America\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Pr
 ivate Bank card and picture ID for access. \n\nAdditional participating m
 useums can be found here: https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-imp
 act/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
