SUMMARY:Fall in the Garden: Planting and Caring for your California Native
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T130000
UID:260930tf1bt5ZzPkW-LrgyDljh3Q
DESCRIPTION:Join Sonoma County Master Gardeners Dandi Hagler and Kim Jacob
 s for a workshop on how to care for your California native plants this fal
 l. \n\nThey'll walk through which plants benefit from pruning now versus 
 later in the season\, and how to identify plants that are setting seed\, w
 hich provide valuable food sources for birds and other wildlife. They'll a
 lso cover broader plant care guidelines to keep your garden healthy year-r
 ound\, along with irrigation strategies for newly installed plants. Whethe
 r you're adding California natives for the first time or maintaining what 
 you already have\, you'll leave with actionable advice on what to do now.
LOCATION:Petaluma Bounty
URL:https://ucanr.edu/site/mg-sonoma/event/fall-garden-planting-and-caring
 -your-california-natives
