X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bikesonom.app.neoncrm.com/forms/basic-first-aid-100626", "Press Democrat": "https://bikesonom.app.neoncrm.com/forms/basic-first-aid-100626"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bikesonom.app.neoncrm.com/forms/basic-first-aid-100626"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Basic First Aid & Scene Management for Bicyclists
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T193000
UID:2609302-NluHp2j0Cf7VEC7x_YfQ
DESCRIPTION:Do you know what to do if there's a crash or medical emergency
  on your group bike ride? Though we might not like to think about it\, a l
 ittle preparation goes a long way. This class will focus on basic "scene m
 anagement" -- how to quickly assess what's happened\, what needs to be don
 e and what you can do to help. We'll talk about what to carry in your on-b
 ike first aid kit\, and things to consider if you're out of cell phone ran
 ge.\n\nLed by our partners at VeloMed\, this class will provide a helpful 
 overview if you're new to these topics or could use a refresher. Pre-regis
 tration is required.
LOCATION:Sonoma County Bicycle Coalition
URL:https://bikesonom.app.neoncrm.com/forms/basic-first-aid-100626
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1385694446333157/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1385694446333157/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1385694446333157/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Foraging Lecture with Dr. Gordon Walker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T180000
UID:2609237UWg6341CUulNXOo-fAIxg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with Dr. Gordon Walker\, author of
  Dr. Fun Guy's Passport to Kingdom Fungi. This event is free\, but we appr
 eciate your RSVP below so we can plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK 
 Learn the basics of fungal biology\, foraging\, and identification in this
  in-depth illustrated introduction from the beloved scientist\, mushroom e
 nthusiast\, and social media star behind Fascinated By Fungi. In Dr. Fun G
 uy’s Passport to Kingdom Fungi\, Dr. Gordon Walker brings his scientific
  knowledge and love for everything fungi to the page. The first section of
  this book is written in a comprehensive question-and-answer format. Start
 ing with “What are fungi?\,” you’ll learn about everything from what
  mycelium is and fungi’s evolution and biochemistry to how they are clas
 sified and how they impact our world today. You will also find information
  on best foraging practices and culinary techniques. The second half of th
 is book introduces you to mushroom identification skills and profiles vari
 ous mushrooms and other fungi\, from incredible edibles you can find in th
 e wild to the dangerously toxic\, medicinal\, and just plain weird. Finall
 y\, you’ll find fungal phenomena\, showing the amazing breadth and diver
 sity of the fungal kingdom. With colorful and comprehensive science illust
 rations\, mushroom photography\, and QR codes linking to resources to help
  you continue your fungal explorations\, this is the perfect portal to ste
 p through into the world of mushrooms. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Dr. Gordon Walker 
 is an award-winning speaker\, science communicator\, published author\, an
 d social media star \\(@fascinatedbyfungi \\) with over 3 million cumulati
 ve followers.  He has a PhD in Biochemistry and Molecular Biology from UC 
 Davis\, where his research focused on the microbial ecology of wine fermen
 tations\, bioprocess control\, and yeast genetics. He is a passionate advo
 cate for mushrooms\, fungal conservation\, and environmental sustainabilit
 y.  His new book "Passport to Kingdom Fungi" will fundamentally transform 
 the way people learn about mushrooms and fungi\, serving as the go-to reso
 urce for a whole new generation of mycophiles and people interested in for
 aging\, wild foods\, and fermentation.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1385694446333157/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
