 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliogr
 aphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\,
  including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details
 : Extra Credit available!This NoodleTools workshop will focus on the MLA A
 PA citation styles.Check with your instructor to confirm the citation styl
 e appropriate for your research assignment.When writing a research paper\,
  the discipline typically determines the citation style you will use.In th
 is workshop\, you will learn how to sign up for an account with NoodleTool
 s. We will also provide examples to show how to create citations\, create 
 a bibliography and check for errors. There will be time to ask questions a
 t the end of the overview —bring your sources along. Join us and learn h
 ow to cite your sources right!Extra Credit: As students\, you have the opt
 ion to submit your instructor and course name when you register if you wou
 ld like us to notify your instructor that you have attended the workshop f
 or extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative 
 way to provide evidence of your attendance.Registration: (click "Begin Reg
 istration" button below)This workshop requires registration in order to be
  admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will receive a confirmation email with t
 he Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam folder if you do not s
 ee it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow you time to l
 og on.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.Not fami
 liar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.Ha
 ve questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T201124Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/noodletools_apa_mla_10
 _5_2026
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citat
 ions and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-w
 riting features\, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs
 .<br />Workshop Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools wor
 kshop will focus on the MLA APA citation styles.<br />Check with your inst
 ructor to confirm the citation style appropriate for your research assignm
 ent.<br />When writing a research paper\, the discipline typically determi
 nes the citation style you will use.<br />In this workshop\, you will lear
 n how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will also provide exa
 mples to show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check fo
 r errors. There will be time to ask questions at the end of the overview 
 —bring your sources along. Join us and learn how to cite your sources ri
 ght!<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your i
 nstructor and course name when you register if you would like us to notify
  your instructor that you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\
 , you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to provide evide
 nce of your attendance.<br />Registration: (click "Begin Registration" but
 ton below)<br />This workshop requires registration in order to be admitte
 d to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will receive a confirmation email with the
  Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see
  it.<br />This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow you time 
 to log on.<br />Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct polic
 y.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a
  Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
