X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.racialjusticeallies.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:THREE YEARS ON: PALESTINIAN GENOCIDE AND SHARED STRUGGLE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T200000
UID:2609202kYk5l6bqUKt5Efy_CEB-g
DESCRIPTION:Palestinian American Tarik Kanaana and Jewish American Carol B
 loom\, both Sonoma County activists\, will share reflections and discuss a
 spects of the 3-year-long ongoing genocide of the Palestinian people.\n\nT
 hey will share personal experiences\, information\, perspectives\, quotes\
 , and poems on a variety of topics\, including:\n\n·       What is 
 it like to be a Palestinian citizen of Israel – a second-class citizen\n
 \n·       The interconnectedness between colonialism\, imperialism\
 , and racism\n\n·       Moving from ignorance/bias to anti-Zionism\
 n\n·       U.S. complicity with Israel and the work of Taxpayers Ag
 ainst Genocide\n\nThere will be ample time for Q&A and discussion among us
 . Invite your friends to join our dialogue. Open to everyone!\n\nEmail rac
 ialjusticeallies@gmail.com to register and we will send you a Zoom link on
  the day of the dialogue.
URL:http://www.racialjusticeallies.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T193000
UID:260415o_McugkyiEKGsztqILBETQ
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.CNPSFall2026.eventbrite.com", "Press Democrat": "http://www.CNPSFall2026.eventbrite.com"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.CNPSFall2026.eventbrite.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Community in Bloom: Botanical Drawing Activity
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T203000
UID:261003u5v2x0Or0kSIHLHjMoNYiQ
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation\, CNPS-Milo Baker Cha
 pter\, and Sonoma County Ag \\+ Open Space for a relaxing evening of drawi
 ng and exploring nature through art. In this hands-on workshop\, participa
 nts will carefully observe a selected plant and learn how to render it usi
 ng colored pencils. With a guided\, step-by-step approach\, even beginners
  will feel comfortable and successful as they create their own botanical d
 rawing to take home.\n\nAfter completing the initial drawing\, participant
 s will have time to add color and detail using colored pencils. Finished a
 rtwork can be framed\, displayed\, or even turned into a blank card for gi
 fting. Most importantly\, the session offers an opportunity to slow down\,
  learn something new\, and enjoy the creative process together.\n\nCareful
  attention to nature can be both calming and nurturing. By closely observi
 ng plants and translating their beauty onto paper\, participants can deepe
 n their connection with the natural world around them.\n\nAbout the Instru
 ctor: Ginny Spencer has been an educator of children and adults for more t
 han 30 years. As a classroom teacher and later as an art instructor for al
 l ages at Oak Grove School\, she has provided a wide range of engaging and
  rewarding art experiences.\n\nOutside the school setting\, Ginny has stud
 ied botanical art using colored pencils with local artist Nina Antze for m
 ore than a decade. She has participated in several art shows\, most recent
 ly an exhibit at Heron Hall featuring plants native to the Laguna environm
 ent.\n\nThere is no charge for this event. It is made possible by the taxp
 ayers of Sonoma County\, who fund the work of Ag \\+ Open Space through a 
 quarter-cent sales tax.
LOCATION:Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation
URL:http://www.CNPSFall2026.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://Sonomahomewine.org", "Press Democrat": "http://Sonomahomewine.org"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://Sonomahomewine.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Mind the Gap: Coastal Climate Impact on Grape Growing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T200000
UID:2610023sOCPACpr0qsHrN1nZxE2A
DESCRIPTION:Mind the Gap: Coastal Climate Impact on Grape Growing \n\nThe
  Sonoma Home Winemakers welcome Ronald Fenolio on October 8\, to discuss
  how coastal fog and marine winds shape world-class vineyard climates up a
 nd down the Pacific coast. Co-founder and owner of Napa’s historic Veede
 rcrest Vineyards\, Fenolio will explore the science of maritime microcli
 mates and show how fog and wind gaps—such as the Petaluma Gap—influenc
 e grape character\, acidity\, and flavor profile. Join us in Room 110 at 
 the Sonoma Community Center\, 276 E. Napa St.\, Sonoma\, CA at 6:30 p.m. 
 to learn how these coastal dynamics define grape sourcing\, varietal selec
 tion\, and wine styles. Admission is free and open to the public\; attende
 es must be 21\\+ for tasting\, and guests are asked to bring their own gla
 ss for shared wine tasting. "Mind the Gap\," the talk dives into the drama
 tic science of coastal microclimates\, revealing how ocean fog and cool ma
 rine breezes drawn through Pacific gaps—like the famed Petaluma Gap—de
 fine grape character\, acidity\, and flavor profile.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:http://Sonomahomewine.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
