X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Remains a Memory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T210000
UID:260930SbYH8h-pHk6bfiFXaJpjew
DESCRIPTION:Remains a Memory- ذكرى تبقى is a still photo collectio
 n from Gaza City\, encapsulating a place\n\nthat holds stories of the land
  and the sea. Within the frames\, serene moments unfold against a\n\nbackd
 rop that longs for genuine peace—a rarity in the artist’s hometown.\n\
 nIn this show\, Lara Aburamadan explores the transformation of memories of
  home shaped by the\n\nrelentless impact of war\, transitioning from tangi
 ble reality to the ethereal realms of daydreams\n\nand nostalgia. Having l
 ived in exile for years\, Aburamadan is left pondering the uncertain path\
 n\nahead\, questioning the fate of a Gaza that clings to memories of peopl
 e and places that don't\n\nexist anymore.\n\nLara Aburamadan is a Palestin
 ian visual artist\, journalist and founder of Refugee Eye. Born\n\nand rai
 sed in Gaza City\, now based in the San Francisco Bay Area\, she tends to 
 embrace the\n\nhuman perspective through visual storytelling. Her photogra
 phs and writings have been\n\npublished in Time Magazine\, New York Times\
 , VICE\, The Atlantic\, NPR\, San Francisco\n\nChronicle\, The Progressive
  Magazine\, AJ\\+\, and elsewhere.\n\nLara has been chosen by Time Magazin
 e among 34 women photojournalists around the world\n\nthat you should foll
 ow their work in 2017.
LOCATION:Autonomous Gallery
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/remains-a-memory/200330
 75/2026-10-09T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
