X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/the-complete-works-of-william-shakespeare/", "Press Democrat": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/the-complete-works-of-william-shakespeare/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/the-complete-works-of-william-shakespeare/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Complete Works of William Shakespeare (Abridged) [Revised] [Ag
 ain]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T203000
UID:260930x7WB5XTqM0Wu_eo07XMIeQ
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare Napa Valley and Napa Valley College bring back the
  laughs with encore performances of *The Complete Works of William Shakesp
 eare (Abridged) \\[Revised\\] \\[Again\\]* by Adam Long\, Daniel Singer\, 
 and Jess Winfield\, with new revisions by Daniel Singer and Jess Winfield.
  Following popular summer performances at di Rosa Center for Contemporary 
 Art’s Shakespeare Summer Stroll\, the production returns indoors to the 
 Napa Valley College Performing Arts Center Studio Theatre for another hila
 rious sprint through all 37 of Shakespeare’s plays. \n\nDirected by The
 ater Arts faculty member Olivia Cowell and starring Theater Arts faculty m
 ember and Technical Director Matthew Cowell\, NVC alum Rio Codda\, and NVC
  student Sofia Quiñones\, three fearless actors tackle Shakespeare’s en
 tire canon with outrageous characters\, rapid-fire costume changes\, physi
 cal comedy\, improvisation\, audience interaction\, and theatrical chaos.
LOCATION:Napa Valley College - Studio Theater
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/the-complete-works-of-william-sha
 kespeare/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
