X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/cana-ranch-uncorked-inaugural-release-party/19658147/2026-10-10T14"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Cana Ranch Uncorked: Inaugural Release Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T170000
UID:260820UYBiUIki8EW1VbZ1oM02iQ
DESCRIPTION:**Cana Ranch Uncorked: Inaugural Release Party**\n\n**Saturday
 \, October 10 | 2–5 PM Hang A Bit Ranch | 2860 Monticello Road\, Napa\, 
 CA 94558 $150 Donation**\n\nJoin Cana Ranch for its inaugural release part
 y\, an intimate harvest gathering celebrating the launch of its first Napa
  Valley Cabernet Sauvignon — and a mission to create meaningful employme
 nt opportunities for adults with intellectual and developmental disabiliti
 es (IDD).\n\nFounded by husband-and-wife team Tyler and Kelly Mullman\, Ca
 na Ranch was created with the belief that wine can be a vehicle for social
  impact. The brand partners with organizations working to expand employmen
 t and job training opportunities for adults with IDD\, with the goal of cr
 eating a sustainable path to meaningful work through the wine and hospital
 ity industries.\n\nAt Cana Ranch Uncorked\, guests will gather for an afte
 rnoon of wine\, food and conversation featuring Cana Ranch winemaker Richa
 rd Frederick and seasonal bites thoughtfully curated by Chef Misty Phelps.
 \n\nThe afternoon will include:\n\nA tasting of Cana Ranch’s inaugural *
 *2024 Cabernet Sauvignon**\, sourced from Tournahu Vineyard in St. Helena\
 n\nSelect wines from Friends of Cana Ranch\n\nSeasonal bites by Chef Misty
  Phelps\n\nA silent auction\n\nRemarks from Cana Ranch founders Tyler and 
 Kelly Mullman\n\nAn introduction to the **WineBev Services** program and i
 ts work creating employment opportunities for adults with IDD\n\n**All pro
 ceeds from the event will support United Cerebral Palsy of the North Bay
 ’s WineBev Services program**\, which provides employment and job-traini
 ng opportunities for adults with intellectual and developmental disabiliti
 es.\n\nCome raise a glass to Cana Ranch’s first vintage and to a future 
 where great wine can help create greater opportunities for everyone.\n\n**
 $150 donation**\n\n**Tickets & Information:** https://canaranch.orderport.
 net/wines/events
LOCATION:Hang A Bit Ranch | 2860 Monticello Road\, Napa\, CA 94558
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/cana-ranch-uncorked-ina
 ugural-release-party/19658147/2026-10-10T14
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
