X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Polenta Feed
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
UID:260924Uw-UGX_ezUilEdBxEsQmJw
DESCRIPTION:Polenta & Stew Dinner – Oct. 10\, 2026 - benefit dinner\n\n
  WHERE:           Penngrove Community Clubhouse\, 385 Woodward
  Avenue\, Penngrove\n\n WHEN:            Saturday\, October 1
 0\, 2026 – Social Hour 5:30 pm\,  Dinner 6:30 pm\n\n TICKETS:    
       $30.00\; children 12 and under $15  - Tickets are by cash or
  check at Soap Cauldron \\(red barn at the end of Penngrove Station\\)\, 
 11830 Main St.\, Penngrove.  \n\nOr online at: https://polenta\\_penngro
 ve.eventbrite.com \n\n WHY:               A benefit for P
 enngrove Park and Clubhouse improvements and the support of our community.
 \n\n CONTACT FOR MORE INFO: Kim Hanson\, \\(707\\) 318- 2191. Or go to h
 ttps://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org\n\n POLENTA AND STEW DINNER BENEFIT
 S PENNGROVE PARK AND CLUBHOUSE – Oct. 10\, 2026\n\n Join us for a cozy 
 evening of hearty polenta and stew\, all for a good cause on\n\nSaturday\,
  October 10\, 2026\, at Penngrove Community Clubhouse\, 385 Woodward Aven
 ue\, Penngrove.  \n\n This is a meal that old-time farmers ate\, long 
 before the term 'farm-to-table' was coined. Polenta and stew will be serve
 d with green salad\, French bread\, and dessert.  \n\n Social hour is a
 t 5:30 pm\, with dinner at 6:30 pm. \n\n All proceeds benefit Penngrove 
 Park and Clubhouse improvements. The nonprofit Penngrove Social Firemen sp
 onsor the event. \n\n Tickets are $30\; children 12 and under are $15. 
  Buy tickets with cash or check at Soap Cauldron\, 11830 Main St.\, or on
 line at  https://polenta\\_penngrove.eventbrite.com\n\n For info\, call
  Kim Hanson at 707 318-2191 or see https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org
 \n\n See more at https://www.PenngroveSocialFiremen.org\n\nhttps://www.in
 stagram.com/penngrovesocialfiremen/\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/groups/339
 347940599\n\nhttps://www.visitpenngrove.com\n\n About Penngrove Social Fi
 remen\n\nPenngrove Social Firemen was formed in 1946 to support the commun
 ity. The non-profit group owns and maintains Penngrove Park and Penngrove 
 Community Club for the enjoyment of all. Members need not reside in Penngr
 ove.
LOCATION:Penngrove Clubhouse
URL:https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
