SUMMARY:Meet + Greet: More Trouble Than It's Worth by Lisa Moore Ramee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T120000
UID:260930dqlOhMyqFEu1iUUgxGEE6w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special meet-and-greet event with Lisa Moore Ram
 ee\, author of More Trouble Than It's Worth. This event is free\, but we a
 ppreciate your RSVP below so we can plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BO
 OK "Ramée successfully weaves themes of friendship\, sports\, social resp
 onsibility\, and family into this engaging coming-of-age story. Shayla’s
  journal features quotations from famous Black women\, a seamless way of s
 haring the insights she gains with readers...A lively novel that explores 
 the inner conflicts and group dynamics that tweens often reckon with." —
  Kirkus Reviews From award-winning author Lisa Moore Ramée comes the comp
 anion to A Good Kind of Trouble\, a heartfelt and powerful sequel about co
 ming of age\, social justice\, and the trials of friendship and competitio
 n\, in which Shayla will learn the true definition of “personal best.”
  After a hard seventh-grade year full of misunderstandings\, face plants\,
  and bullies\, all Shayla wants is a hassle-free summer. Her ticket to a s
 ummer of fun? Joining the club track team! However\, Shayla struggles to f
 it in with new friends\, to set a personal best that will secure her a spo
 t in the exclusive Junior Olympics\, and reluctantly earns the title of 
 “Prank Queen.” But Shayla discovers that sometimes trying so hard to s
 tay out of trouble ends up making things a whole lot worse. Will she risk 
 new friendships by owning up to a big mistake? And is she ready to speak o
 ut against another social injustice? In this powerful and heartfelt follow
 -up to A Good Kind of Trouble from acclaimed author Lisa Moore Ramée\, Sh
 ayla will learn the true definition of personal best. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Lis
 a Moore Ramée was born and raised in Los Angeles and now lives in Norther
 n California with her husband\, daughter\, obnoxious cat\, and rambunctiou
 s \\(but sweet\\) dog. She's a devout believer in dreams coming true and i
 s the author of A Good Kind of Trouble\, a Walter Dean Myers Honor Book\, 
 The Everybody Experiment\, Something to Say\, and MapMaker. You can visit 
 her online at lisamooreramee.com.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/27815061771469203/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
