 or InfoinfoFAQprogram overviewTataki-zomé is the practice of pounding a f
 lower or leaf into fabric\, leaving a detailed\, semi-permanent print. In 
 this workshop\, participants will work with a selection of seasonal and lo
 cally sourced botanicals and transfer them onto upcycled linens to create 
 whimsical prints of their design. We will also learn about natural dye bas
 ics\, including permanence\, care\, and the difference between colorfast a
 n
LOCATION:Redwood Grove\, 276 East Napa Street\, Sonoma\, California
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/flower-pounding/
