END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T173000
UID:260831McaQYeVCA0Ko0rqYogF0nQ
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T170000
UID:260212IaPcE-HuA06eOVX3q-GNdA
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on **Sunda
 ys from 4:00 – 5:00 PM** **at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulu
 pa Ave.\, Room #4\, Santa Rosa**. Contact: Abigail (707) 293-5888. You may
  view all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northb
 ayoa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emoti
 onal\, and physical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and livi
 ng by their spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a d
 iet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of e
 ating.\n\nOA does **not** endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is ca
 using problems in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery
  is possible\, and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa
 .org/\n\n**Find a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
