DESCRIPTION:The Petaluma Cinema Series is a unique\, film education progra
 m that mixes the Santa Rosa Junior College campus community with residents
  of Sonoma County to screen and discuss significant classic and modern cin
 ema. Within the series\, our Filmmakers in Conversation program regularly 
 hosts directors\, actors\, and motion picture technicians.  Guest evenings
  are generally structured with a 6pm talk or filmmaker interview\, a 7pm s
 creening\, and a question &amp\; answer session following the film.  The p
 rogram is hosted in the Carole L. Ellis Auditorium on the SRJC Petaluma Ca
 mpus. Films are projected in 4K with 7.1 sound.For more information\, visi
 t the Petaluma Film Alliance website. (https://petalumafilmalliance.org/20
 26-fall-schedule/)&#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T193730Z
LOCATION:Carole L. Ellis Auditorium - SRJC Petaluma Campus
