SUMMARY:Sound of Our Stories - Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T130000
DTSTAMP:20260829T092312Z
UID:20261015T190000Z-23939@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T120000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,251,251/407_PET_intercultural_center_graphic_3.rev.1
 756413439.png
CATEGORIES:Intercultural Center
DESCRIPTION:Join us each month for the Sound of our Stories Campus Communi
 ty Luncheon. The monthly series will create a recurring\, student-led perf
 ormance space where participants are invited to center their cultural iden
 tities\, lived experiences\, and creative traditions through dance\, music
 \, spoken word\, poetry slam\, storytelling\, and other expressive art for
 ms. Each event will be free and open to the SRJC community and hosted on c
 ampus.  Students who perform will be given a $50 incentive.Sign up to perf
 orm! (https://santarosajuniorcollege.formstack.com/forms/sounds_of_our_sto
 ry)Sounds of Our Story website. (https://petaluma.santarosa.edu/sounds-our
 -story)  This campus community event is funded by a grant from the Santa R
 osa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowmen
 t.  All are welcome to attend!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T181027Z
LOCATION:SRJC Petaluma Cafe Patio
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23939-sound-of-our-stories-open-m
 ic
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us each month for the Sound of our 
 Stories Campus Community Luncheon. The monthly series will create a recurr
 ing\, student-led performance space where participants are invited to cent
 er their cultural identities\, lived experiences\, and creative traditions
  through dance\, music\, spoken word\, poetry slam\, storytelling\, and ot
 her expressive art forms. Each event will be free and open to the SRJC com
 munity and hosted on campus.</p><p>  Students who perform will be given a 
 $50 incentive.</p><p><a href="https://santarosajuniorcollege.formstack.com
 /forms/sounds_of_our_story" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sign up to perf
 orm!</a></p><p><a href="https://petaluma.santarosa.edu/sounds-our-story" t
 arget="_blank" rel="noopener">Sounds of Our Story website.</a></p><p>  Thi
 s campus community event is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior C
 ollege Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.</p><p>  A
 ll are welcome to attend!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:23939
