BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-10-17/karen-gebbia-meet-greet", "Press Democrat": "https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-10-17/karen-gebbia-meet-greet"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-10-17/karen-gebbia-meet-greet"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Karen Gebbia Kids Event Meet & Greet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:260924qhN9K9eOy0y05BrcOZW69g
DESCRIPTION:Join us to celebrate Karen Gebbia's new picture book about wai
 ting patiently! And we'll be serving sweet tea as only our manager can mak
 e it\, so you won't have to wait for that!\n\nSo\, what's it about?\n\nCha
 rlotte wants to wait patiently. She really does. But waiting is hard\, esp
 ecially on a stifling Maryland morning\, when her t-shirt feels like a hot
 \, heavy blanket\, and she can't think of anything but Nana's cold\, sweet
 \, lemony\, real iced tea.\n\nThere are so many steps to Nana's secret rec
 ipe tea! Steeping\, sugaring\, cooling . . . baking muffins to go with it!
  Nana tells her to find something useful to do while she waits\, so Charlo
 tte sweeps\, and swings\, and snaps pillowcases\, but it still isn't ready
 !\n\nCharlotte has to find more things to do to pass the time\, and soon s
 he finds that a day spent waiting can be a day spent enjoying the slower m
 oments. Sometimes the sweetest things in life are the things we have to wa
 it for\, and learning to savor them slowly is a joy all its own. Included 
 is a reader's note for adults on helping kids learn how to wait and a secr
 et recipe to try at home.\n\nAuthor info!\n\nKaren Gebbia is a children's 
 book writer and naturalist based in California. Before writing for childre
 n\, Karen spent two decades writing\, publishing\, editing\, and teaching 
 scholarly writing.
LOCATION:Copperfield's Books- Petaluma
URL:https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-10-17/karen-gebbia-meet-greet
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.marinmommies.com/calendar/pumpkins-pikes-0"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Pumpkins on Pikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
UID:260923YWlOCXMyh0CA-K4nMynMsw
DESCRIPTION:In addition to producing healthy and sustainable local food\, 
 Petaluma's  Tara Firma Farms also puts on fantastic family-friendly events
  throughout the year. Come on out to the farm for Halloween fun with pumpk
 in carving\, live music\, a straw maze\, games\, food\, drinks\, and more.
  Pumpkins on Pikes takes place on Saturday\, October 17 and 24 and Sunday\
 , October 25\, from 2 to 9 pm. The festivities start in the afternoon with
  great food\, live music and pumpkin carving. Everyone will get the chance
  to display their Jack-O-Lantern on a pike in the corn field. When the sun
  goes down the pumpkins are lit. It is a truly heart warming feeling looki
 ng over the glowing corn field to see the individual creations of all who 
 attend. Free pumpkins for carving will be provided with admission. Bring y
 our pumpkin carving tools\, blankets and coats to stay warm after dark\, a
 nd a sheet to cover hay bales for seating. Admission is $40 and includes a
  carving pumpkin. Children 3 and under are admitted free \\(no pumpkin pro
 vided\\). Tickets must be ordered in advance and are not available at the 
 door.
LOCATION:Tara Firma Farms
URL:https://www.marinmommies.com/calendar/pumpkins-pikes-0
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
