BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/indigenous-voices-series-sherrie-smith-ferri/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Indigenous Voices Series: Sherrie Smith-Ferri
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T203000
UID:260715h1_4XOAru0CqlNRbO-5JLA
DESCRIPTION:Indigenous Voices Series: Sherrie Smith-Ferri is known In Heal
 dsburg for curating the Healdsburg History Museum's From Diggers Bend to R
 iver Rock: Dry Creek Rancheria People and History. She also created the Fo
 ley Pavillion history display for Dry Creek Rancheria Band of Pomo and Wap
 po peoples. For THE 222\, this nationally known scholar and storyteller wi
 ll launch an essential new book based on her knowledge. She will share his
 torically important and entertaining stories about growing up in Healdsbur
 g and Dry Creek from her perspective as a Pomo citizen. Her experience as 
 a basketmaker\, with all its cultural associations\, adds layers to her po
 pular presentations.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/indigenous-voices-series-sherrie-smit
 h-ferri/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
