SUMMARY:Retos en las Montañas (Challenges in the Mountains) #3
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T150000
UID:260917s-VYtPmCJ0CmVX0o4aKfEA
DESCRIPTION:Join Jack London Park Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff
  in a series of intermediate hikes\, guided in Spanish\, between Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Each hike is a roun
 d trip\, returning to the starting point\, and will increase in length or 
 difficulty. Not appropriate for children under 12 years old.\n\nSat. Oct. 
 24 – Upper Fallen to Camp Via to Fern Lake at Jack London. 5.72 miles\, 
 1\,150 ft. elevation \\(meet at Jack London State Historic Park\\).\n\nSat
 . Nov. 7 – Gunsight Rock at Sugarloaf/Hood Mountain Regional Park. 6.44 
 miles\, 2\,129 ft. elevation \\(meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\\).\n\n
 Sun. Nov. 15 – Sonoma Ridge in Sonoma Developmental Center/Jack London. 
 9.67 miles\, 2\,126 ft. elevation \\(meet at the intersection of Arnold Dr
 . and Harney Rd.\, inside the SDC\\).\n\nSat.  Nov. 21 – "The Big Loop"
  at Sugarloaf. 7.37 miles\, 1\,739 ft elevation \\(meet at Sugarloaf Ridge
  State Park\\).
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
