BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomavalleypride.com/events/rocky-horror-picture-show-at-sebastiani-theater-50th-anniversary-screening-and-costume-contest/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomavalleypride.com/events/rocky-horror-picture-show-at-sebastiani-theater-50th-anniversary-screening-and-costume-contest/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomavalleypride.com/events/rocky-horror-picture-show-at-sebastiani-theater-50th-anniversary-screening-and-costume-contest/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Rocky Horror Picture Show With Full Shadow Cast and Costume Contes
 t
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T223000
UID:2609062g9niJnBUE2L53yjFdUlGA
DESCRIPTION:**Don’t dream it. Be it!**\n\nSonoma Valley Pride is bringin
 g **The Rocky Horror Picture Show** back to the historic Sebastiani Thea
 tre for our **second annual screening and costume contest** — and this
  year\, we’re taking it to a whole new level.\n\nFor the first time\, Ro
 cky comes to life with a **full shadow cast performed by San Francisco’
 s Bawdy Caste**!\n\nWatch the cult classic on the big screen while a live 
 cast performs along with the film right in front of you. Expect outrageous
  audience participation\, **props for throwing**\, ridiculous costumes\, 
 plenty of callbacks\, and a costume contest celebrating your very best Roc
 ky Horror looks.\n\nWhether you’ve been doing the Time Warp for decades 
 or this is your first trip to Frankenstein Place\, come ready for a night 
 of camp\, chaos\, community\, and absolute fun.\n\n**All proceeds benefit 
 Sonoma Valley Pride!** \n\n**Schedule**\n\n**6:30 PM — Doors Open**\n\nC
 ome early\, grab your seat\, show off your look\, and get ready for the ni
 ght.\n\n**7:00 PM — Pre-Show & Costume Contest**\n\nWe’ll kick things 
 off with our costume contest\, pre-show festivities\, and all the preparat
 ion you need before the madness begins.\n\n**7:40 PM — The Rocky Horror 
 Picture Show + Live Shadow Cast**\n\nThe film begins with **SF’s Bawdy 
 Caste performing live alongside the movie.**\n\n**Guests are highly encour
 aged to come dressed as their favorite Rocky Horror character** — or si
 mply embrace the spirit of the night and wear something fabulous\, outrage
 ous\, strange\, glamorous\, or completely over the top.\n\nPrizes will be 
 awarded to some of our favorite looks of the evening.\n\nAnd yes — **au
 dience participation is strongly encouraged.**\n\n**Remembering a Legend**
 \n\nThis year’s screening will be especially bittersweet following the p
 assing of **Tim Curry**\, whose unforgettable portrayal of Dr. Frank-N-Fu
 rter helped make *The Rocky Horror Picture Show* the cultural phenomenon
  it is today.\n\nFor generations\, Rocky Horror has permitted people to be
  louder\, stranger\, freer\, more theatrical\, and more unapologetically t
 hemselves.\n\nThis October\, we’ll gather together to celebrate Tim Curr
 y\, the character he made iconic\, and the enduring spirit of individualit
 y\, freedom\, and queer joy that continues to make Rocky Horror so meaning
 ful.\n\nSo grab your fishnets\, warm up your Time Warp\, gather your frien
 ds\, and join Sonoma Valley Pride for one unforgettable night at the Sebas
 tiani Theatre.\n\n**SF's Bawdy Caste**\n\nThe Bawdy Caste is San Francisco
 ’s legendary Rocky Horror shadow cast\, bringing glitter\, fishnets\, ir
 reverence\, and unapologetic camp to stages across the Bay Area and beyond
  for three decades.\n\nMore than a performance troupe\, The Bawdy Caste ce
 lebrates individuality\, acceptance\, and community. Their stage is a spac
 e where people can be loud\, strange\, expressive\, and fully themselves 
 — creating an inclusive environment where everyone is encouraged to feel
  seen\, welcomed\, and part of the fun.
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
URL:https://sonomavalleypride.com/events/rocky-horror-picture-show-at-seba
 stiani-theater-50th-anniversary-screening-and-costume-contest/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108002647?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Blue Note Napa Summer Sessions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T000000
UID:260612aqZUUyax4Ea8sqKSk5NGXA
DESCRIPTION:It’s been a full quarter-century since a young saxophonist a
 nd composer released his debut recording as a leader\, Trust. On September
  1\, 2017\, Boney James released his 16th album\, this one titled Honestly
 . If you sense a direct line between those titles\, you’ve already come 
 a long way toward understanding what motivates the four-time GRAMMY nomine
 e and multi-platinum-selling musician.\n\n“I’m fighting the good fight
  to be my own artist and not be pigeonholed\,” says the genre-blurring J
 ames. “With a record’s title I always try to find something that will 
 communicate the feeling I get when I listen to it. The feeling I get with 
 this music is a sense of sincerity and intimacy. The word ‘honestly’ r
 eally reflects how I aspire to live my life and create my music. These are
  interesting times we are living in and the one thing I can do with the sk
 ills that I have is to make music that evokes a feeling and takes people s
 omewhere… to do what I can to try and make the world a more pleasant pla
 ce.”\n\nHonestly follows futuresoul\, James’ 2015 release which spent 
 eleven weeks at \\#1 on the Billboard Contemporary Jazz Chart. The New Yor
 k Times raved\, “Boney James performs with panache...His arc as a solois
 t is emotional...he can paint a scene.” Honestly\, says James\, is quite
  different sounding than the previous record. “It’s more exposed\,” 
 he says of the 10-track collection. “A number of the songs have a more b
 uoyant\, cheerful\, happy quality to them.” James produced the record an
 d co-wrote all but one track\, his interpretation of the Johnny Mercer-Hoa
 gy Carmichael classic ‘Skylark.’\n\nHis skill as a performer as well a
 s a recording artist garnered this notice from the Boston Globe\, “James
  swaggered across the stage like a blacktop hero draining treys on an over
 -matched opponent. He even weaved his way through the audience\, never mis
 sing a beat and all but daring the crowd not to have a good time."\n\nOver
  the years\, James has racked up sales of more than three million records\
 , four RIAA gold albums\, four GRAMMY nominations\, a Soul Train Award\, n
 ominations for two NAACP Image Awards and 10 CDs atop Billboard’s Contem
 porary Jazz Albums chart. In 2009\, Billboard named him one of the Top 3 C
 ontemporary Jazz Artists Of The Decade along with Kenny G and Norah Jones.
 \n\nWith Honestly\, as with futuresoul and the GRAMMY-nominated The Beat b
 efore it\, Boney James is making some of the most stellar\, wholly realize
 d music of his career. “I’ve just grown up\, personally and musically\
 ,” he says. “I’m a lot calmer now when I approach making music and h
 ave more confidence. I’m a “give-110 percent” kind of person and I
 ’m enjoying the process more now. I think that comes out in the music. M
 aybe that’s why this new record is so much fun to listen to. There are p
 arts on the record that still make me smile.”
LOCATION:The Meritage Resort and Spa
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108002647?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/patrick-ball-celtic-harp-story-1", "North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/patrick-ball-celtic-harp-story-1"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/patrick-ball-celtic-harp-story-1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Patrick Ball: Celtic Harp & Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T210000
UID:6a8c9c573787652e870acdcd@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Step into the enchanting world of\nPatrick Ball\n\, one of the
  premier Celtic harp players in the world and a captivating storyteller wh
 ose performances weave music\, legend\, wit\, and wonder into an unforgett
 able experience.\nWith the crystalline beauty of the Celtic harp as his mu
 sical voice\, Ball brings ancient Irish tales and timeless melodies vividl
 y to life\, transporting audiences to a world of heroes and dreamers\, mys
 tery and mischief\, heartbreak and humor. His masterful playing and gift f
 or storytelling create an evening that is at once intimate\, magical\, and
  deeply human.\nJoin us at Occidental Center for the Arts for a spellbindi
 ng journey through the music and stories of Ireland with a true master of 
 the tradition.\nTickets are $35\, $30 for OCA members. Doors open at 6:30 
 PM\, refreshments available. Art gallery open during event.\nGet Tickets\n
 About Patrick Ball:\nWhether in the stronghold of a Galway chieftain in th
 e years before history began or yesterday in the snug corner of a pub in D
 ublin\, the Irish have always delighted in storytelling. Their passion for
  eloquence and wordplay\, their deep devotion to their mythical past\, the
 ir ability to find joy and humor in a dark world\, and their belief that t
 he supernatural world could appear between one breath and the next made th
 eir stories and the telling of them unrivaled in the world of the oral tra
 dition.\nAnd always\, amidst the storytelling\, there was music. Jigs\, re
 els and haunting airs graced the spaces between the tales. And first among
  Irish instruments\, and the most honored\, was the legendary Celtic harp.
  With its crystalline\, bell-like voice and lavish resonance\, it would so
 othe its listeners and lead them deeper into the realms of the imagination
 .\nIn\nCeltic Harp and Story\nPatrick Ball rekindles the fire and wonder o
 f an evening of Irish storytelling. For in telling the marvelous old tales
  of wit and enchantment\, and in playing the ancient\, brass-strung harp o
 f Ireland\, he not only carries on two of the richest traditions of Celtic
  culture\, but blends them in concert to create “a warm and magical perf
 ormance.”\n“An American master of the Irish instrument\, a peripatetic
  modern day bard\, combining tale-telling\, history and music into a seaml
 ess compound that reaches all ages and types of listeners.”—San Franci
 sco Chronicle\n“It’s rare that we will feature a performer on our fine
  performances season for two consecutive years\, but then Patrick is a rar
 e artist ... The audience was entranced by his harp playing\, amused by hi
 s storytelling. Patrick is a grand man who puts on a great show.”—APAP
  Report / Humboldt State University\n“The SRO audience loved Mr. Ball's 
 performance\, asking when we will be bringing him back. Ball was a delight
  to work with\, very professional\, and he is superb at captivating an aud
 ience.”—APAP Report / Arizona State University\n“Patrick Ball conjur
 ed some Druid magic ... weaving words and music into a spellbinding progra
 m.”—The Blade\, Toledo\, OH
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/patrick-bal
 l-celtic-harp-story-1
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
