SUMMARY:Little Shop of Horrors The Broadway Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T170000
UID:260930Hw-uAe4iWUOi7eLMlDBltA
DESCRIPTION:Step into the wild\, witty world of “Little Shop of Horrors
 ”\n\nFeed the need for musical mayhem! The cult-classic smash hit LITTLE
  SHOP OF HORRORS is coming to Bay Area Stage Theatre on Broadway! Meet Sey
 mour\, Audrey\, and the most outrageous plant ever to take over a stage. P
 acked with unforgettable songs\, dark comedy\, romance\, and outrageous th
 rills\, this wildly entertaining musical will have audiences screaming for
  more!\n\nCast and crew - Victor Barajas: Seymour\, Joanna Lynn Costa: Aud
 rey\, Nathaniel Mercier: Orin Scrivello \\(The Dentist\\)\, Scott Slagle: 
 Mushnik\, Justin Daily: Voice of Audrey II\, Perris O'Neil: Urchin/Ronette
 \, Isabella Percy: Urchin/Crystal\, Maizzy Patton: Urchin/Chiffon\, Shanno
 n Tallchief: Ensemble\, Ava Butcher: Puppeteer and Rehearsal Assistant\, L
 orenzo Servente: Puppeteer\, Brian Sennello: Music Director\, Jeff Lowe: D
 irector\, Stacey Loew: Costume Designer\, Julia Blair: Assistant to the Di
 rector.
LOCATION:Bay Area Stage Theatre
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/906875162504849/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.singnapavalley.org", "Press Democrat": "http://www.singnapavalley.org"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.singnapavalley.org"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sing Napa Valley presents “American Songbook Singer Showcase”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T170000
UID:260923jAGPQhdGdE2ZgiApSNu4UA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s musical heritage with Sing Napa Valley a
 t the *American Songbook Singer Showcase*. Presented in honor of the Unite
 d States’ 250th anniversary\, this lively afternoon concert travels from
  the 1920s through the early 1960s with jazz standards\, Broadway favorite
 s\, and memorable songs from film. Two concerts: Saturday\, October 24 & S
 unday\, October 25 at 3pm.\n\nWhether these classics are lifelong favorite
 s or brand-new discoveries\, *American Songbook Singer Showcase* promises 
 an uplifting celebration of music’s power to bridge generations and brin
 g people together.\n\nEnjoy timeless music by George and Ira Gershwin\, Co
 le Porter\, Hoagy Carmichael\, and Irving Berlin\, including favorites suc
 h as “Mr. Sandman\,” “Honeysuckle Rose\,” “Night and Day\,” an
 d “Dream a Little Dream of Me.” Sing Napa Valley choir members and spe
 cial guests will take the spotlight in solos\, duets\, trios\, and small e
 nsembles\, joined by collaborative pianist Anthony Mayor. Bring family and
  friends for an uplifting celebration of music that connects generations.
LOCATION:American Legion Hall
URL:http://www.singnapavalley.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/adrian-west-band/19964471/2026-10-25T15"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Adrian West Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
UID:2609211HnixvFkpUya-zmop3hP7A
DESCRIPTION:The six-piece Adrian West Band will perform from 3 - 5pm with 
 an intermission in the Atrium room of the Osher JCC. Will include Joe Esco
 bar on the Grand Piano. Ticketed show. Details coming soon.\n\nAdrian West
  Band is a six-piece acoustic rock ensemble from Oakland. They play a fun 
 mix of originals\, covers and instrumentals plus some popular Jazz standar
 ds. Some describe their sound as “Paul Simon meets Talking Heads”.\n\n
 A native of Montreal\, Adrian enjoys setting philosophical lyrics to uplif
 ting music. Whether telling a story about a skinny-dipping episode gone aw
 ry or grappling with the many challenges facing humanity\, his lyrics are 
 fueled by equal parts hope\, realism and whimsy and ride atop a steady wav
 e of catchy music.\n\nCovers and standards the band will play will include
  some or all of these: Ants Marching (Dave Matthews) Brass In Pocket (The 
 Pretenders) Closer to Fine (Indigo Girls) Feels So Good (Chuck Mangione) A
 rmando’s Rhumba (Chick Corea) Happy People (Kenny Garrett) Linus & Lucy 
 (Vince Guaraldi)\n\nInstrumentation: 2 vocalists\, acoustic guitar\, elec.
  violin\, piano\, upright bass\, alto sax\, drums\, percussion\, live loop
 ing\n\nAdrian West - vocals\, acoustic guitar\, elec. violin & live loopin
 g Joseph Escobar on piano Amy Obenski - vocals\, percussion Chris Haag - a
 lto sax Aaron Germain - upright bass Dan Foltz - drums\n\nFor more informa
 tion\, visit www.adrianwest.com
LOCATION:Osher Marin JCC
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/adrian-west-band/199644
 71/2026-10-25T15
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
