SUMMARY:Liam St. John & Bridge City Sinners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T190000
UID:260910WluCVIlB70q_hL2z-aJphA
DESCRIPTION:Liam’s debut full-length project\, “stripped back” \\(Ju
 ne 2022\\) reached \\#1 in Top Blues Albums globally on Apple Music\, foll
 owed up by a successful nationwide tour that wrapped with a sold out show 
 in Music City\, USA. \n\nAt the crossroads of the blues and rock & roll\, 
 Liam St. John commands his truest form by combining lyrics that embody the
  blues with their piercing and painful truth\, and delivering a captivatin
 g performance with vibrancy true to the spirit of rock and roll. Liam floo
 ds the room with an electrifying energy\, washing over every stage he grac
 es. \n\nSt. John made his mark in Nashville after inking with King Pen Mus
 ic by way of Warner Chappell at the end of 2022. This is the blues-crooner
 ’s first publishing deal.  “I was knocked out by Liam‘s voice when I
  first heard it.  He is such a creative and unique artist with a vision li
 ke no other. His music brings a fresh new look on blues and rock in this w
 orld”\n\nLiam credits his foundation for singing to the legends he grew 
 up listening to. From Ray Charles to Etta James\, Sam Cooke\, Louis Armstr
 ong\, and Tracy Chapman\, the raw\, gritty\, blues-infused soul always sur
 faces in Liam’s songs and performances. \n\nLiam is managed by Aidan Cro
 wley with Legacy Content. //
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108686729?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
