X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/AItools_10_28_26"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Navigating Research with AI Tools at SRJC Libraries @ 4pm\, Oct 28
 th
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T170000
DTSTAMP:20260918T133126Z
UID:20261028T230000Z-24037@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T160000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour.rev.178605768
 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:AI apps can empower researchers to discover topic connections 
 and identify areas for further exploration. Librarian Canon Crawford will 
 focus on responsible research practices and academic integrity while explo
 ring AI tools at SRJC Libraries.Workshop Details: Extra Credit available!E
 xtra Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor a
 nd course name when you register if your instructor is offering extra cred
 it and you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attended.
  Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to provide e
 vidence of your attendance.Registration: (click "Begin Registration" butto
 n below)This workshop requires registration in order to be admitted to the
  Zoom meeting.You will receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link
  for this workshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see it.This Zoom 
 workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.Attendees 
 are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? 
 Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Ch
 at with an SRJC Librarian!
