X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:AI apps can empower researchers to discover t
 opic connections and identify areas for further exploration. Librarian Can
 on Crawford will focus on responsible research practices and academic inte
 grity while exploring AI tools at SRJC Libraries.<br />Workshop Details: E
 xtra Credit available!<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the optio
 n to submit your instructor and course name when you register if your inst
 ructor is offering extra credit and you would like us to notify your instr
 uctor that you have attended. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an
  alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Registration
 : (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />This workshop requires re
 gistration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will rece
 ive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check y
 our spam folder if you do not see it.<br />This Zoom workshop will open 10
  minutes early to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees are asked to ab
 ide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch thi
 s 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? Chat 
 with an SRJC Librarian!
