SUMMARY:Pumpkins in the Park: A Santa Rosa Scavenger Hunt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T180000
UID:260923oi_wma5Cn0ijN3JaCpn2Vw
DESCRIPTION:Think you know our City parks well enough to be able to find t
 he rare pumpkin cutouts?! Here’s how it works… --- DETAILS - Beginning
  Oct. 1\, visit any one of our City parks from the link below and hunt for
  pumpkin cutouts! - Pumpkin cutouts will be eight inches tall and laminate
 d on card stock. - If you find a pumpkin cutout\, the directions on how an
 d where to collect your prize will be on the back \\(also listed below\\).
  The first day you can collect a prize is Oct. 1. - Staff will re-hide the
  pumpkin cutouts for others to find \\(last date of re-hiding is Oct. 23\\
 ). - Oct. 30 will be the last day you can collect a prize for finding a pu
 mpkin cutout. --- MORE INFORMATION Visit SRCity.org/PumpkinHunt for more i
 nformation\, including a list of City parks where pumpkin cutouts will be 
 hidden\, how to collect your prize\, and more.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1941397493189788/1941453906517480/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T130000
UID:260924PffdXbjk-0KrpyaY0RB5Ag
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free\n\nSponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of 
 summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn th
 at was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over ju
 st to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, ra
 w milk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Speci
 alty prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market.\n\nEn
 joy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal p
 lace to meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover
  the abundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Far
 mers Market\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your do
 llar into a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footp
 rint\, and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food 
 by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine
 .\n\nwww.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T170000
UID:260914tW6kDCCzt0S1N4OAgu-tjg
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present *“Antarctica: The 
 Frozen Desert\,”* a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\,
  opening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November. 
  The exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after
  more than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity
 \, he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar reg
 ions. The exhibit features work generated over 6 *voyages to the* Antarcti
 c Peninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Fal
 klands and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photogra
 ph.\n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on
  Earth\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely
  outside of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of 
 years ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 year
 s. Defined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — 
 vast\, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a 
 kind of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever be
 fore.
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "http://www.pomoproject.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T163000
UID:2609092SbOoMFnuUGwN92Qnh_iEg
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Nataraja School Of Traditional Yoga": "https://www.meetup.com/nataraja-school-of-traditional-yoga/events/gmtbbvyjcnbmc/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_nataraja_school_of_traditional_yoga
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Nataraja Yoga
UID:event_gmtbbvyjcnbmc@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050415Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T103000
SUMMARY:Yoga Vinyasa & Pranayama
DESCRIPTION:Nataraja School of Traditional Yoga\n**Yoga Vinyasa Krama - Th
 ursdays 9-10:30am**\n**Songbird Community Healing Center Cotati**\n**RSVP 
 ONLY**\nPhysical Health\, Conditioning\, Pranic Flow\, Vital Energy\, Ment
 al Focus & Stillness - through intelligent architecture with the metaphysi
 cs of deep conscious breathing & slow motion\, yogic breathwork\, mantra/s
 ound/vibration\, mudra\, subtle & contemplative practices.\nYoga Vinyasa K
 rama is a comprehensive hatha-raja yogic system for purification\, develop
 ing concentration\, neuromuscular fitness and conditioning\, refining & ma
 stering the breath\, awakening subtle energy and stilling the mind. Based 
 on deep breathing & the subtle movement of prana directed into the cartila
 ge tissue\, sinuous musculature\, internal organs\, nerve pathways and nad
 is. It has over 700 intelligently sequenced slow\, conscious breath powere
 d with precision movement variations with pause (vinyasas)\, exploring man
 y aesthetic variations of each posture to correctly establish the main asa
 nas while the mind merges with the breath.\nIncludes the energetics of dri
 shti\, pratikriyas\, bandha\, vaseth\, mudra\, mantra\, surya & ding namas
 kar with breath & mantra\, cleansing kriyas\, Himalayan pranayama includin
 g including ujjayi variations\, heating & cooling breaths\, solar\, lunar 
 & soli-lunar nadi shuddhi practices\, pranava & samantraka pranayama\, pra
 tyahara\, subtle & contemplative practices in 12 kramas (sequences).\nThe 
 whole process gradually transforms the body and mind\, releasing old patte
 rns of physical and mental tension and dysfunctional patterns of movement\
 , providing tonic\, energetic and psychophysiological effects.\nThis syste
 m is presented from the teachings **Srivatsa Ramaswami** learned through h
 is over 33 years of one on one study with **Sri Krishnamacharya** and teac
 hings from a similar **Himalayan method**.\nThis ongoing class will explor
 e the entire system of 12 Kramas with each class focusing on a particular 
 krama or vinyasas from different kramas & pranayama & dharana practices.\n
 Please practice on an empty stomach. Morning beverage ok but please take i
 t 30min or more before class.\n***Certain injuries & health issues may be 
 contraindicated Please contact me if you have a concern***\nKnowledge of U
 jjayi Breathing recommended\n**$25 Drop In\, Discounted Class Passes\, Sli
 ding Scale Available**\n\\*\\***RSVP Only** Contact Kara @707-235-1413\, [
 breathprayeryoga@protonmail.com](http://sunyogadance@gmail.com%2A%2A/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/nataraja-school-of-traditional-yoga/e
 vents/gmtbbvyjcnbmc/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260904T024534Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T024534Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
