DESCRIPTION:Join Certified California Naturalist John Lynch on a “spooky
 ” 3 mile\, 3.5 hour hike from Creekside to Hillside and back through the
  meadow exploring this very special season. With Halloween around the corn
 er\, we might just discover witches' butter\, flying saucer galls\, zombie
  leaves\, plants that have been skeletonized\, or even some “ghostly“ 
 sheet web spiders. Have the bats been using their bat house\, let’s find
  out. We’ll also see if we can identify some of the “treats” of the 
 season (seeds\, nu
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Road\, Kenwood\, C
 A 95452
