CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:The Petaluma Cinema Series is a unique\, film education progra
 m that mixes the Santa Rosa Junior College campus community with residents
  of Sonoma County to screen and discuss significant classic and modern cin
 ema. Within the series\, our Filmmakers in Conversation program regularly 
 hosts directors\, actors\, and motion picture technicians.  Guest evenings
  are generally structured with a 6pm talk or filmmaker interview\, a 7pm s
 creening\, and a question &amp\; answer session following the film.  The p
 rogram is hosted in the Carole L. Ellis Auditorium on the SRJC Petaluma Ca
 mpus. Films are projected in 4K with 7.1 sound.For more information\, visi
 t the Petaluma Film Alliance website. (https://petalumafilmalliance.org/20
 26-fall-schedule/)&#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T193323Z
LOCATION:Carole L. Ellis Auditorium - SRJC Petaluma Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23956-exit-8-fall-cinema-series
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Petaluma Cinema Series is a unique\,
  film education program that mixes the Santa Rosa Junior College campus co
 mmunity with residents of Sonoma County to screen and discuss significant 
 classic and modern cinema. Within the series\, our Filmmakers in Conversat
 ion program regularly hosts directors\, actors\, and motion picture techni
 cians.</p><p>  Guest evenings are <em>generally</em> structured with a 6pm
  talk or filmmaker interview\, a 7pm screening\, and a question &amp\; ans
 wer session following the film.</p><p>  The program is hosted in the Carol
 e L. Ellis Auditorium on the SRJC Petaluma Campus. Films are projected in 
 4K with 7.1 sound.</p><p><a href="https://petalumafilmalliance.org/2026-fa
 ll-schedule/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more information\, visit 
 the Petaluma Film Alliance website.</a>&#160\;</p>
