SUMMARY:Reg Rodriguez - Human Agency & Machine Inquiry
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T120000
DTSTAMP:20260903T102413Z
UID:20261113T190000Z-23946@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T110000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,500,500/710_cs_-_ai-speaking-series-wilde-500x500.pn
 g.jpg
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:As generative AI becomes embedded across disciplines\, higher 
 education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle between opposing camps\, 
 but of intentional design.  Generative systems offer novel capabilities fo
 r research\, creation\, and learning\, yet their ultimate value depends en
 tirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.Reg Rodriguez serves as subject m
 atter expert evaluating the quality and accuracy of AI-generated legal con
 tent.Learn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website. (https://c
 s.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T175426Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23946-reg-rodriguez-human-agency-
 machine-inquiry
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  As generative AI becomes embedded across
  disciplines\, higher education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle bet
 ween opposing camps\, but of intentional design.</p><p>  Generative system
 s offer novel capabilities for research\, creation\, and learning\, yet th
 eir ultimate value depends entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.</p>
 <p><strong>Reg Rodriguez</strong> serves as subject matter expert evaluati
 ng the quality and accuracy of AI-generated legal content.</p><p><a href="
 https://cs.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lea
 rn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website.</a></p>
