BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Novel Lovers Of Sebastopol": "https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/316660565/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_novel_lovers_of_sebastopol
X-SOURCE:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County
UID:event_316660565@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050417Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261226T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261226T143000
SUMMARY:Yesteryear by Caro Claire Burke (option 2)
DESCRIPTION:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County\, CA\nA modern day Christian tra
 dwife Natalie decides with her husband to take the family to live in a far
 mhouse\, grow their own food\, raise chickens and a cow\, and raise/home s
 chool their ever-increasing brood without modern influences. However -- mo
 m is also a social media influencer who videos everything... except the na
 nnies and farmworkers behind the scenes. She wakes up one day and she and 
 some version of her family are in a real farmhouse (with no helpers) in 18
 55! How to get out of this nightmare/delusion/time travel?\n\n"I found it 
 to be a realy page turner--couldn't put it down. I definitely think that w
 e should read this for our group. It's so unusual and I think it would pro
 vide fodder for very interesting discussion." - Nancy R.\n\n"For the life 
 of me\, I can’t figure out why I kept reading this book given that most 
 of the characters in it are deplorable. But I sure kept reading it. And th
 en when I finished it\, I wondered what kind of a person could write such 
 a book and I was surprised when I listened to the interview that the autho
 r is actually full-fledged human being with a heart and a sense of humor. 
 To me\, that the sign of someone with tremendous craft. There are many top
 ics in this book that I think would be a wealth for us to discuss: The dou
 ble lives of social media influencers\, Tradwife vs Girlboss\, can we go b
 ack into the way that used to be. I suspect the reason this book is so hot
  because it’s so topical." - Lucinda\n\n"It took me a bit to get into (I
  was just so annoyed at the beginning:) but after things began to develop\
 , I was hooked. A lot to discuss - although it may be tough to separate ou
 t discussion on the book itself and the real-world implications!" - Debra\
 n\n"[Why You Should Read ‘Yesteryear’ Now](https://www.nytimes.com/202
 6/05/10/briefing/yesteryear-caro-claire-burke.html?unlocked_article_code=1
 .01A.Gak9.SZGpJviEJq74&smid=url-share)" - NY Times\n\n"‘[Yesteryear’ i
 s this summer’s must-discuss book. We have questions.](https://www.washi
 ngtonpost.com/style/interactive/2026/06/18/yesteryear-is-this-summers-must
 -read-book-let-discuss/)" - Washington Post
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/316
 660565/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260922T053305Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T053305Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
